{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>These are the words which Moses spoke.</b> As it is said: ״מוכיח אדם אחרי חן ימצא ממחליק לשון״ — 'A man who rebukes will afterward find favor, more than he who smooths the tongue.' מוכיח אדם — this is Moses, who rebuked Israel, as it is said: ״ואתנה צאני צאן מרעיתי אדם אתם״." "<b>Ahar.</b> After the Holy One, blessed be He, rebuked them, and because he rebuked them — חן ימצא, as is said of Moses: ״וגם מצאת חן בעיני״." "<b>More than he who smooths the tongue.</b> This is Balaam, who spoke to them smooth things and said: ״מה טובו אוהליך יעקב״. A parable of Moses and Balaam — to what may the matter be compared? To a king's son who has two ministers, one who loves him and one who hates him. The one who loves him says to him: My son, be careful lest you transgress, for your father is king and judge, and if he hears, he will not spare you but will kill you. The one who hates him says: Do every desire of your heart, for the king is your father, and you need not fear anything. Thus Moses, the one who loves, said to Israel: ״השמרו לכם פן יפתה לבבכם״, and it is written: ״וחרה אף ה׳ בכם״ etc. But Balaam, the one who hates, said to them: ״מה טובו אוהליך יעקב משכנותיך ישראל״ etc. — and do every desire of your hearts, for concerning the nations He does all the evil that He decreed upon them, as it is said: ״לא איש אל ויכזב״. But concerning you, since you are His children — even if He decreed an evil matter, He said of them ״ולא יעשה ודבר ולא יקימנה״. And concerning them Solomon said: ״נאמנים פצעי אוהב ונעתרות נשיקות שונא״. And concerning Moses too it is said: ״ולמוכיחים ינעם״ — and upon them will come blessing of good, but concerning him it is not said except ועליהם — upon the one who rebukes and upon the one who accepts rebuke." "<b>Between Paran and between Tophel and Lavan.</b> Words of vanity (תפלות) that they uttered against the manna, which was white (לבן). And what would they say? Can there be one who grinds yet does not excrete — for they eat the manna and it is absorbed in the limbs?"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:32.622714517Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}